  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "El acusativo: lo que se tiene",
    "@en": "The accusative: what you have"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "Lo que recibe la acción del verbo va en **acusativo**. La buena noticia: solo cambia el **masculino**. **Ein** pasa a **einen**: **Ich habe einen Bruder** (tengo un hermano).",
     "@en": "What gets the verb's action is in **acusativo**. The good news: just change the **masculino**. **Ein** passes to **einen**: **Ich habe einen Bruder** (I have a brother)."
    },
    {
     "@es": "El femenino y el neutro no cambian: **eine Schwester**, **ein Kind**.",
     "@en": "feminine and neutral do not change: **eine Schwester**, **ein Kind**."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Para decir que no tienes algo se usa **kein**, que cambia igual: **Ich habe keinen Bruder**, **Ich habe keine Schwester**.",
     "@en": "To say you don't have something **kein** is used, which changes the same: **Ich habe keinen Bruder**, **Ich habe keine Schwester**."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "tabla",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Nominativo y acusativo",
    "@en": "Nominative and accusative"
   },
   "filas": [
    [
     "sujeto (nominativo)",
     "ein Bruder",
     "eine Schwester",
     "ein Kind"
    ],
    [
     "objeto (acusativo)",
     "einen Bruder",
     "eine Schwester",
     "ein Kind"
    ],
    [
     "negación (acusativo)",
     "keinen Bruder",
